From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Abel Vesa <abel.vesa@linaro.org>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 17:53:25 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 19/20] soc: qcom: pmic_glink_altmode: use a freezable
 workqueue for the altmode worker

Abel Vesa <abel.vesa@linaro.org>, posted to linux-arm-msm.

  Fixes: 080b4e24852b ("soc: qcom: pmic_glink: Introduce altmode support")
  Cc: stable@vger.kernel.org    # 6.3

pmic_glink_altmode_worker() runs on system_wq, which is not frozen for
suspend, so it can reach a Type-C retimer, switch or mux over i2c while the
i2c controller is still suspended. Queue it on system_freezable_wq instead,
so it does not run until the devices have resumed.

Observed upstream on X Elite (ParadeTech PS8830); the same warning appears
here on the Fairphone 5 via the ucsi connector change path, fixed by the
companion patch ucsi-connector-change-on-freezable-wq.

The hunks below are regenerated against this tree, whose line numbers differ
from the posted patch.

Signed-off-by: Marcus Ramberg <marcus@means.no>
---
 drivers/soc/qcom/pmic_glink_altmode.c | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/soc/qcom/pmic_glink_altmode.c b/drivers/soc/qcom/pmic_glink_altmode.c
index 13c434f8d03a..465e5d2316a0 100644
--- a/drivers/soc/qcom/pmic_glink_altmode.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/qcom/pmic_glink_altmode.c
@@ -451,7 +451,7 @@ static void pmic_glink_altmode_sc8180xp_notify(struct pmic_glink_altmode *altmod
 	alt_port->mode = mode;
 	alt_port->hpd_state = hpd_state;
 	alt_port->hpd_irq = hpd_irq;
-	schedule_work(&alt_port->work);
+	queue_work(system_freezable_wq, &alt_port->work);
 }
 
 #define SC8280XP_DPAM_MASK	0x3f
@@ -502,7 +502,7 @@ static void pmic_glink_altmode_sc8280xp_notify(struct pmic_glink_altmode *altmod
 		alt_port->tbt_data = *tbt;
 	}
 
-	schedule_work(&alt_port->work);
+	queue_work(system_freezable_wq, &alt_port->work);
 }
 
 static void pmic_glink_altmode_callback(const void *data, size_t len, void *priv)
